Subject: search from the location bar, a start page, Reload and Home buttons,
 maximized

What a desktop browser is expected to have. Words typed in the location bar (anything with a space,
or one word without a dot, slash or colon, localhost aside) become a search: BADWOLF_SEARCH_URI,
DuckDuckGo's HTML results, which need no scripts. The start page is BADWOLF_HOME_PAGE
(<datadir>/start.html, which the package ships; WALNUT_BROWSER_HOME=<URI> overrides it, about:blank
when neither is there): opened at start without arguments, in a new tab and by the new Home button
(Alt+Home after the next patch), with the location bar left empty for typing. A Reload button
next to back and forward. The window starts maximized: on a TV the browser is the whole screen.
uri_test covers the search cases.

